# Node config field system

JSON-driven config drawer for project flow nodes. Schema files live in `node-config/schemas/<kind>.json`; field rendering in `ProjectNodeConfigField.tsx`.

## Field types (`ProjectConfigFieldType`)

| Type | Renders as | Editable |
|------|-----------|----------|
| `text` | Plain `<Input>` | ✅ with `bind` or `optionKey` |
| `mono` | Monospace `<Input>` | ✅ |
| `textarea` | `<Textarea>` | ✅ |
| `url` | Editable `<Input>` or clickable link | ✅/read-only |
| `secret` | Password `<Input>` with eye-toggle | ✅ requires `optionKey` |
| `toggle` | `<Switch>` | ✅ requires `optionKey` |
| `select` | `<NativeSelect>` + static `options[]` | ✅ |
| `llm_provider` | Provider select from catalog | ✅ |
| `llm_model` | Model select filtered by provider | ✅ |
| `source_plugin` | Plugin select from profiles | ✅ |
| `variable_key` | Variable select | ✅ |
| `image` | Read-only image tag + Upgrade button | — |
| `hint` | Muted help text | — |

## Field binding

```json
{ "bind": "host" }        // writes to top-level ProjectNode prop
{ "optionKey": "port" }   // writes to node.options["port"]
{ "resolve": "image" }    // read-only computed value
```

**`bind` targets:** `label`, `subtitle`, `host`, `detail`, `agentPrompt`

A field needs **either** `bind` or `optionKey` to be writable. Also set `"editable": true`.

## Credential section pattern

For `postgres`, `redis`, `github` nodes — use tab `"credentials"` (opened by default) with `"id": "credentials"` section:

```json
{
  "id": "credentials",
  "labelKey": "projects.config.sections.credentials",
  "tab": "credentials",
  "fields": [
    { "id": "host",  "labelKey": "projects.config.fields.host",     "type": "mono",   "bind": "host",          "editable": true, "placeholderText": "127.0.0.1" },
    { "id": "port",  "labelKey": "projects.config.fields.port",     "type": "text",   "optionKey": "port",     "editable": true, "placeholderText": "5432" },
    { "id": "db",    "labelKey": "projects.config.fields.dbName",   "type": "text",   "optionKey": "dbName",   "editable": true },
    { "id": "user",  "labelKey": "projects.config.fields.username", "type": "text",   "optionKey": "username", "editable": true },
    { "id": "pass",  "labelKey": "projects.config.fields.password", "type": "secret", "optionKey": "password", "editable": true, "hintKey": "projects.config.credentialHint" }
  ]
}
```

**`secret` field** stores in `node.options`; renders as `type="password"` with eye-toggle. Use for passwords, API tokens (`token` optionKey), and signing secrets.

## Tabs and sections — available IDs

**Tabs:** `parameters` | `source` | `network` | `credentials` | `variables` | `settings` | `export` | `output`

**Sections:** `trigger` | `source` | `networking` | `credentials` | `scale` | `deploy` | `model` | `memory` | `tools` | `scrape` | `export` | `danger` | `overview` | `prompt` | `agent-settings` | `keys` | `fields` | `proxy`

## i18n keys for credential fields

All defined in `en.ts` / `zh.ts` / `km.ts` under `projects.config`:

```
projects.config.tabs.credentials
projects.config.sections.credentials
projects.config.fields.port
projects.config.fields.dbName
projects.config.fields.dbIndex
projects.config.fields.username
projects.config.fields.password
projects.config.fields.accessToken
projects.config.showSecret
projects.config.hideSecret
projects.config.credentialHint
```

## Adding a new field type

1. Add the type string to `ProjectConfigFieldType` union in `node-config/types.ts`
2. Add a renderer branch + sub-component in `ProjectNodeConfigField.tsx` (follow `SecretField` pattern)
3. Update the relevant `<kind>.json` schema
4. Add i18n keys to all three locale files
